    "correctAnswer": "a",
    "explanation": "i. r = 3/(-1) = -3 ✓\nii. nth term = (-1) × (-3)^(n-1) = (-1)(-3)^(n-1)\nFor this to equal (-3)^(n-1), we need n=1 to give -1, but (-3)^0 = 1, not -1.\nActually: -1, 3, -9, 27, ... = (-1)(-3)^0, (-1)(-3)^1, (-1)(-3)^2,...\nSo nth term = (-1)(-3)^(n-1) ≠ (-3)^(n-1) for n=1.\nStatement ii is FALSE ✗\niii. S₆ = (-1)(1-(-3)^6)/(1-(-3)) = (-1)(1-729)/4 = (-1)(-728)/4 = 182 ✓\nSo i and iii are correct, answer should be b) i and iii.\n# Corrected Questions\n## Question 19:",
